  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nUpper ridging becomes centered over north Texas Wednesday evening. \nThis feature then strengthens and meanders toward the Desert \nSouthwest through the remainder of the week and into the weekend. As \na result, hot and mostly dry conditions are expected to persist \nthrough the rest of the Long Term period. Triple digit heat \nexpands to include more portions of the Permian Basin, the Upper \nTrans Pecos, and southeast New Mexico Thursday afternoon compared \nto Wednesday afternoon. Friday and into early next week, triple \ndigit heat shall dominate most of our region, with the exception \nof 90s in the higher terrain and adjacent areas. Highs look to \nreach or exceed 105 degrees near and along the river valleys and \nportions of the Permian Basin most afternoons. The hottest \nconditions will be along the Rio Grande in the Big Bend this \nweekend, where highs could range between 110-115 degrees. Lows \ngenerally fall into the 70s each night. Aside from isolated showers/\nstorms near the elevated terrain in west Texas and portions of \nsoutheast New Mexico, most locations will remain dry.",
